# The peer resends its SYN (our SYN-ACK was lost): it is answered at once,
# and the SYN-ACK timer counts again from that answer -- no timer SYN-ACK
# right behind it.  A third SYN within 500 ms of the answer gets none.
# The ACK of the answer's TSval (the first SYN's, as before) completes it.
# Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project
0.000 socket s stream
0.000 bind s 8080
0.000 listen s 16
0.100 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
0.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
0.900 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 900 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
0.900 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
1.200 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 1200 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
1.900 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
2.000 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 2000 ecr echo>
2.000 accept s c
2.010 state c ESTABLISHED
